  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts` for the candy-red clearcoat car on a turntable. It passes `typecheck`, but I couldn't run it in a browser or run `vite build`, so I haven't seen a rendered frame. Look at a capture before trusting the look.\n\n- **Car:** The body, cabin and roof panel are smooth shapes generated in code, with seam-averaged normals. The cabin is dark glass, and the roof is painted. Chrome tubes follow the body and cabin belt lines. There are four rubber wheels with chrome rims and caps.\n- **Paint:** `material.carPaint` supplies a deep red base coat and a glossy clear coat. A flake normal map generated in code (`texture.data`) adds the fine sparkle. I couldn't tell whether the engine applies that normal map to custom meshes, so the sparkle is the part most likely to look wrong.\n- **Lighting:** The reflections come from `environments.neutral` plus three long rect lights (overhead, left, right). A cool rim light sits behind, with a faint bloom. Three emissive fixture bars hang above the set. They are not reflected in the paint, because I avoided the untested environment-capture route.\n- **Turntable:** The platform is a semi-transparent dark glass disc with a glowing ring light and tick marks. Under the glass is a darker mirrored copy of the car, which gives the faint floor reflection. I used the copy because I didn't trust screen-space reflections without a way to test them.\n- **Camera and state:** The camera is fixed, low and front-three-quarter. The turntable turns at 20° per second, measured with `performance.now()`. `window.__TASK_STATE__` is updated every frame with the unbounded angle and `paintFinish: 'clearcoat'`. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set two animation frames after `app.ready()`.",
